Newton, Jacobians, continuation and solver evidence (@pe-power-flow-solver: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/MATPOWER-User-Manual-8-1.lingua#r_5ANPNGQHP93EVQXR6FW357WSEV", #source "../sources/Three-Phase-Unbalanced-Networks-Das.lingua#r_4J5TZVPWY0FYP8WY7AGZM8NQ4B", #source "../sources/Introduction-to-Applied-Linear-Algebra-Boyd.lingua#r_3684D74C735KQS61ST3EH0XKZW", #electrical-power-engineering "../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8") { r_2KM2RZT4E5AY1HNQWXJGBXBQ6H
**Read:** [MATPOWER User’s Manual, version 8.1](../sources/MATPOWER-User-Manual-8-1.lingua#r_5ANPNGQHP93EVQXR6FW357WSEV), chapters 4–5 in full; [Three-phase unbalanced networks — Biswarup Das](../sources/Three-Phase-Unbalanced-Networks-Das.lingua#r_4J5TZVPWY0FYP8WY7AGZM8NQ4B), complete detailed Newton/Jacobian sequence; [Introduction to Applied Linear Algebra — Boyd and Vandenberghe](../sources/Introduction-to-Applied-Linear-Algebra-Boyd.lingua#r_3684D74C735KQS61ST3EH0XKZW), conditioning, least-squares and linear-system methods.

Derive the mismatch equations and Jacobian for a small power-flow system. A Newton step solves a local linear approximation; damping, initial conditions, scaling and stopping criteria influence convergence. Small residuals prove satisfaction of the stated equations within numerical accuracy, not uniqueness or physical suitability of the model.

Compare analytic derivatives with an independent finite-difference check over a justified perturbation range. Test known limits, alternative initial states and a second formulation. Separate equation residual, update size, constraint violations and discontinuous bus/control logic. An unconverged result must not be presented as a physical state merely because its voltages look plausible.

Use continuation to trace a solution branch through loading, with a declared parameterization and event/limit treatment. Near a fold, the ordinary Jacobian becomes ill-conditioned and sensitivity increases; a different parameterization can still follow the mathematical branch. Distinguish voltage-solvability limits from dynamic voltage stability. The original two-bus calculation provides an exact restricted branch benchmark before the complete multibus methods and independent advanced investigations.

**Continue:** [Build a numerical validation argument across several kinds of evidence](../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
